why: The composition of the tiers lives ONLY in okay.demo.IntentRouter
  — cue tier first, vector tier below it, escalate under the margin,
  fill the frame from the message, ask what is missing. That order is
  the measured one, and a caller outside the demo has to re-derive it
  by reading twenty Results sections. okay-intent should hold the
  composed door, with the demo as its caller rather than its
  definition.

shape: a value the caller builds once (taxonomy, cues, an optional
  model, an optional embedder, floors) and calls per message. It
  answers with a class, a filled frame, the question still to ask, or
  the candidates it could not separate — the same four outcomes the
  demo already proved are the right ones.

now possible: intent-fitted-model-ships landed, so the default door
  can carry Models.meeting and answer with no network at all.

